! pH acid: 0.1 M HNO3; pH base: 0.1 M KOH
! Water level: automatic constant level in supply tank
! Nutrient dosing: MANUAL daily at 16:00h based on measured NO3 and uptake ratios
! NOTE: System volume = 168.0 L (measured, cv=1.3%)
! NOTE: Final system volume = 176.4 L (5% increase due to root mat water retention)
! NOTE: Gully geometry (Heinen et al. 1991): 12 gullies x 326.5 cm long x 23.5 cm wide x 4.0 cm deep, slope 1:75 (S-facing)
! NOTE: Greenhouse area = 9.21 m2 (12 x 3.265 m x 0.235 m), derived from gully geometry
! NOTE: PPOP = 15.64 plants/m2 (156,400/ha); 144 plants / 9.21 m2 = 15.6; in-row spacing ~27.2 cm (326.5 / 12)
! NOTE: SOLVOL = 18.2 mm = 168 L / 9.21 m2; CHLEN = 326.5 cm; = 23.5 cm from gully geometr
! NOTE: NO3C/PC/KC/CAC/MGC/SC corrected 2026-08-04 to match Heinen 1994 (Rapport 1, exp 6705) Table 2.1
!       set points (mmol/L: NO3 5.000, P 0.333, K 2.624, Ca 1.172, Mg 0.392, SO4-S 0.168),
!       converted to mg element/L. Previous values (82.2/11.7/126.2/100.2/18.2/120.1) were wrong:
!       Ca and Mg matched the OTHER Heinen experiment (1991 paper, exp 5132, 2x concentration),
!       and S was ~22x too high versus either source.

! NOTE 2026-11-06: SVOL is read as mm depth by IPEXP.for; 168 L / 9.21 m2 = 18.2 mm (was 168.0, 9x too large).
! NOTE 2026-11-06: PLWT restored to measured 1.87 kg/ha (12 mg/plant x 15.6 plants/m2); was 1.00.
! NOTE 2026-11-06: PLWT 1.40 kg/ha = 9.0 mg/plant x 15.6 plants/m2. Heinen Tbl 3.1 week 0: shoot dry 0.007 g; root dry 0.005 g at 14.15% d.m. is likely inflated by sand (seedlings sown on sand), so root dry taken as root fresh 0.033 g x 6% (later harvests 5.8 to 6.9%) = 0.002 g.
